WEBVTT

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:08.580
An insurer, a mutual or a public payer
works with hundreds of practices,

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:11.900
each with its own software, and
cannot compare their results.

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:16.160
Dental Data gives it consistent data
from the whole network

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:19.680
without centralising records: the
computation happens in

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:23.880
each practice and only the
aggregated result comes back.

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:27.240
The same applies to public dental
programmes and reforms,

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:29.660
which will have to measure their outcomes.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:34.720
With clear limits: the European Health Data
Space prohibits using these data

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:40.040
for advertising or for decisions that harm
people, including in insurance.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:45.170
Consistent data from the whole network,
without centralising records.
